  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transition from informality to formality for vulnerable groups, including refugees, migrants and domestic workers, promoted</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Turkiye in 2023, the total number of unregistered employed people is around 8.2 million. The unregistered employment rate has fallen to 26.1% in 2023 from 34.8% in 2019. Unregistered employment is considerably higher in the agricultural sector (80.6%). In addition, women are more prone to be employed unregistered (32.2% total; 90.6% in agriculture). Informality is considerably higher among refugees. In order to tackle informality, the ILO is working with the Social Security Institution for the implementation of the &apos;Transition to Formality (KIGEP)&apos; programme to ensure formal employment and job retention of Syrian, non-Syrian and host community workers in certain project provinces. The ILO is also working on supporting the cooperatives to increase their resilience in the labour market as well as ensuring their transition to formality.</narrative>
  </description>
